<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  Product overlay for SettingsProvider's Settings.Global and Settings.System
  defaults. Only the three values below are overridden; everything else keeps
  the AOSP default, because a DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS resource file is merged
  per resource name rather than swapped in whole.

  These defaults apply to a FRESH userdata only. SettingsProvider seeds
  Settings.Global and Settings.System once, on the first boot of an empty
  /data. On a board whose /data is already provisioned, set the same values
  live instead:

      settings put global window_animation_scale 0
      settings put global transition_animation_scale 0
      settings put global animator_duration_scale 0    (no resource default
                                                        exists; runtime only)
      settings put system screen_off_timeout 1800000

  def_window_animation_scale / def_window_transition_scale = 0%
    Window and transition animations are pure compositor work on a platform whose
    GPU is not the bottleneck: with three Settings/Home transitions driven in a
    loop, V3D render sat at about 24% while DomD's device model burned 83% of a
    core translating and copying frames. Turning the two scales off removes that
    work from every screen change. Measured together with loglevel=4 and
    Bluetooth off: DomD went from 120.4% to 89.6% of a core over the same
    workload. Set them to 50% instead of 0% if the demo wants the motion back at
    half the cost.

  def_screen_off_timeout=1800000  (60 s to 30 min)
    This panel has no backlight, so the dim step of the screen off sequence is
    applied as a near black overlay (DisplayPowerController brightness 0.397 to
    0.05) and the display simply looks dead. Measured on the board 2026-09-16:
    after a menu had been left on screen for 112 s, every tap was consumed as a
    wake event, so not one button press reached the app underneath. The same
    dim made A2DP playback look like the screen going black several times. This
    default covers the whole UI (Bluetooth audio, settings, the launcher) and
    survives a userdata wipe, which a runtime `settings put` does not.

  Note for editors: XML comments may not contain a double hyphen, which is why
  this block uses none.
-->
<resources>
    <fraction name="def_window_animation_scale">0%</fraction>
    <fraction name="def_window_transition_scale">0%</fraction>
    <integer name="def_screen_off_timeout">1800000</integer>
</resources>
